# whitelist file for block-badips
#
# Each IPv4 or IPv6 address which is in a separate line will never be blocked
# by block-badips.sh, even if it is on the downloaded list or in
# /etc/block-badips.blacklist. Ranges are not supported.
# Lines containing anything else, like these comments, are ignored.
#
# Examples:
#192.0.2.10
#2001:db8::10
127.0.0.1
